  "text": "It makes complete sense that you feel that way; when the pressure is on to choose a \"safe\" or traditional path, pursuing art and writing can definitely feel risky.\n\nHowever, it's worth remembering that what feels practical often changes depending on how we define success. Many people who ended up in creative fields initially worried exactly about this—whether they could make a living from their passions or if it was too uncertain. Sometimes, taking small steps in an area you love (like writing a short story or sketching daily) can help clarify not just what you enjoy, but also how those interests might fit into a future plan without feeling like a gamble.\n\nHave you ever thought about ways to blend your interest in art or writing with other subjects, or perhaps explored what kinds of roles exist in those fields today?",
